  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nElections - Wayne County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n Wayne County, Iowa\n \nElections\n \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n \n\n \n \nHome\n \nVote \n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections \n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials \n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n Wayne County\nElections\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nWelcome to the Wayne County Elections Website.\n The Auditor’s Office is responsible for every aspect of conducting an election from voter registration to the final count of the votes. This site is designed to be a resource for residents looking to learn how to vote, find their elected officials, learn about becoming a candidate, or find past or upcoming election information.\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \nQuick Links\n \nRegister to Vote\n \nWhere Do I Vote?\n \nAm I Registered?\n \nHow Do I Vote?\n \nElection Results\n \nElected Officials\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nUpcoming & Recent Elections\n \n\n \n\n \nNov\n \n3\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election\n General Election\n \n\n Election Information Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nSep\n \n8\n \n \n\n LOSST Special Election\n Special Election\n \n\n Unofficial Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nJun\n \n2\n \n \n\n 2026 Primary Election\n Primary Election\n \n\n Official Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n News\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\nAll News\n \n \n\n \n FAQ\n \n\n \nQ.\n \n\nCan I register to vote on Election Day?\n \n\n \n \n\n \nA.\n \n\nYes. Iowa law allows for Election Day registration if you are able to provide proof of identification (i.e. valid photo ID) and proof of residency (i.e. utility bill with your name on it if your ID has an outdated address on it). If you are unable to provide one or both of these you are allowed to bring someone with you to attest that you have the right to vote. \n\n \n\n \n \nAll Frequently Asked Questions\n \n \n\n \n Wayne County Voter Registration\n \n\n Updated October 2, 2026\n \n\n\n \nRepublican\n \n\n\n \n2,188\n \n\n \nNo Party\n \n\n\n \n971\n \n\n \nDemocratic\n \n\n\n \n586\n \n\n \nOther Party\n \n\n\n \n23\n \n\n \n \n \nTotal Registered Voters: 3,768\n \n Register to Vote\n \n \n\n\n\n\nThis webpage was printed on October 17, 2026. For the most current election-related information, visit the \".$clientCounty.\" County, Iowa, Elections website at REPLACE_THIS.\n\n\n \n\n Wayne County Courthouse\n\n 100 N Lafayette Street\n \nP.O. Box 435\n \nCorydon, IA 50060\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n\n Wayne County Website\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n 8:00 AM - 4:00 PM\n \nMonday - Friday\n \n \n \nPhone Number\n\n (641) 872-2242\n \n \n \n\n \n\n >Facebook Contact Us\n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n>powered by \n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
